schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Mercy Corps Ventures cut delivery costs 60% using stablecoins in Syria
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Mercy Corps Ventures cut delivery costs by 60% by using stablecoins
    instead of traditional money transfers in Syria.
  evidence: Cited to cryptoaltruism.org (CryptoAltruists Web3 Impact Toolkit).
  source_lineage: CryptoAltruists Web3 Impact Toolkit (as cited in the article)
  interpretation: >-
    Used as the article's concrete "everyday operations" proof point for
    stablecoins beyond emergency crisis fundraising.
  uncertainty: >-
    Single-source figure with no methodology given for how the 60% cost
    reduction was calculated; not independently verified here.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/case-studies-nonprofits.md
    transformation: quoted
    authorship: ai-assisted
  notes: |
    # assessed-but-excluded
    - Ukraine 2022 emergency-fundraising narrative (banks froze, $50M+ raised
      in bitcoin, UkraineDAO) — read and considered for its own claim-evidence
      entry, but excluded as a duplicate of the same "web3 = fast disaster
      infrastructure" claim already covered structurally by this entry and the
      encyclopedia-entry summary; flagging here rather than silently dropping.
    - Direct quotes from named individuals (Tammy Tibbetts of She's the First;
      CryptoAltruists commentary) — kept as quoted text inside claim-evidence /
      encyclopedia-entry fields, not turned into standalone public person-nodes
      (per the do-not-create-public-person-nodes rule).
    - "Try This" action-prompt section — operational/coaching text, not a
      knowledge object; not extracted.
